{
  "name": "WF5 Publish (due)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### WF5 — Auto-publish\nEvery 15 minutes. Calls `/api/cron/publish-due`, which:\n\n1. **claims** due rows with one conditional `UPDATE … RETURNING` — two overlapping\n   runs cannot post the same row twice;\n2. resolves the channel (member's own Buffer channel, else the page's);\n3. publishes and marks — **`published` only when Buffer returned a post id**.\n\nBuffer answers **HTTP 200 for a failed mutation**, so the app never reads the status\ncode as success (`P01`, `SC09`). This workflow does not decide anything; it rings\nthe bell.\n\nG4 still exists — it lives in `agent_schedule.gate_status`. A Pro member's first\nthree publishes sit at `g4_review` until a human moves them to `pass`.\n\n**Requires:** `JARVIS_BRAIN_URL`, `CRON_SECRET` in n8n Variables.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "5253cbb1-70b7-5239-a94f-c0a5af0ecaa6",
      "name": "README",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -380,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "cronExpression",
              "expression": "*/15 * * * *"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "07f4725c-fb16-5cd9-88ab-7beef36b739e",
      "name": "Every 15 min",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $vars.JARVIS_BRAIN_URL }}/api/cron/publish-due",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "Authorization",
              "value": "=Bearer {{ $vars.CRON_SECRET }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "timeout": 120000
        }
      },
      "id": "a55c86ac-ce17-55e1-a311-f66de0fdce8c",
      "name": "POST publish-due",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        230,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "did",
              "leftValue": "={{ ($json.published || 0) + ($json.failed || 0) > 0 }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "458e088d-24c9-5160-972c-455cba4797f2",
      "name": "Anything happened?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        460,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const d = $input.first().json;\n// Only speak when something actually moved. A 15-minute 'nothing due' ping is\n// how a notification channel gets muted, and then the one real failure is missed.\nconst lines = [];\nif (d.published) lines.push(`${d.published} published`);\nif (d.failed) lines.push(`${d.failed} failed`);\nconst retries = (d.results || []).filter(r => r.outcome === 'retry');\nif (retries.length) lines.push(`${retries.length} retrying`);\nreturn [{ json: {\n  quiet: lines.length === 0,\n  text: lines.length\n    ? `WF5 — ${lines.join(', ')} of ${d.claimed} claimed.`\n    : 'nothing moved',\n  detail: (d.results || []).filter(r => r.outcome !== 'published'),\n} }];"
      },
      "id": "9a1e2469-23ee-524e-b3a5-8334ad37b63c",
      "name": "Summarise",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        680,
        -80
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "chatId": "={{ $vars.TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID }}",
        "text": "={{ $json.text }}",
        "additionalFields": {}
      },
      "id": "f2b74e72-7c6b-5ce6-aa1b-ec6f72135222",
      "name": "Telegram Sir",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegram",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        900,
        -80
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "telegramApi": {
          "id": "REPLACE_TELEGRAM",
          "name": "Jarvis Bot"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
